MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_001: Fianna! Hello there.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_002: Aah! No!
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_003: Fianna? What's the matter? You look scared.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_004: Wait...was it me? Did I scare you?
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_005: I...I don't think it was you. But I can't be certain.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_006: I know there's something special about you.\nAnd I know you're kind.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_007: But I just got the sudden feeling that I was in danger\nof losing someone close to me.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_008: It's just a feeling... I'm sorry I reacted the way I did.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_009: You don't need to apologize, Fianna. I know from\nexperience that the human heart is complicated.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_010: Sometimes I also feel things that don't seem quite\nlike myself. It can be confusing.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_011: Oh, Orchel, I had no idea...
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_012: Uh-huh. I'm just like you that way.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_013: The person you're afraid to lose is Talimun, right?\nDo you like him?
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_014: So there's someone you're afraid to lose...do you\nlike this person a lot?
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_015: I do. He's strong, won't be tied down, and lives his\nlife to its fullest... I feel safe around him.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_016: Heh. No need to worry, then. He doesn't sound like\nhe's in danger of being taken away.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_017: I fear I am not so certain...
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_018: He attracts women wherever he goes. I worry he may\nwander off with one of them, never to be seen again.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_019: If those are the ties he avoids, I see why you're\nworried. But I still think everything will be alright.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_020: After all, they say a pegasus tramples the head of\nany who would trample a heart.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_021: That poor pegasus...
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_022: Oh, it's just a figure of speech! But you're very\nkindhearted to worry about its feelings.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_023: But don't you feel sorry for the pegasus, having to\ndole out punishments to all those villains?
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_024: Good point. I bet the pegasus would indeed not be\nvery happy about it.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_025: Why can't they simply be struck by lightning?
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_026: You're right. That's much better! Let's pray for the\nscoundrel to get struck by lightning.
MID_SE_Orh_Fia_C_027: Heehee. Thank you. That is some relief...
